<%#
  One collapsible role section of the project Files panel — also what renders the Backups,
  Repositories-adjacent Linked-from-elsewhere and (via the folder loop) every ROLE_LABELS group.

  Locals: key (a stable slug for the section, unused below but kept for a caller that wants one),
  label, rows (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Row), open (Boolean).

  A ROW IS A FOLDER FILE OR A LINKED ATTACHMENT, AND row.linked? IS THE ONLY BRANCH IN THIS
  PARTIAL. A folder row's node comes straight from the listing's own walk and carries no
  attachment at all (row.attachment is nil) — there is nothing to detach and nowhere else in the
  library the file already lives, so its tile is the thumbnail alone. A linked row's node is
  attached to this project but living somewhere else in the library, so its tile also carries a
  corner: Detach (severs the reference; the file itself is kept) and Move into project
  (Maker::AttachToProject#relocate under the file's own name — the same door the collision
  prompt's "Move it in as…" button posts to, in _move_conflict.html.erb).

  EXTRACTED BECAUSE THERE ARE NOW SEVERAL CALLERS — one per role, Backups, and Linked — and they
  must render identically apart from being open or closed and carrying that one corner or not.
  Inlining any of them was the obvious thing and would have meant one more copy of the tile
  markup, which is how the Detach/Move corner ends up on some of them and not the others.

  `open` is a real HTML attribute, so a closed section costs nothing at render time and the browser
  keeps the toggle state for the life of the page. It is NOT persisted across loads: that would need
  a cookie per section per project, and the panel's default (everything open but Backups) is the
  answer for almost every visit.
%>
<section class="attachment-group">
  <details <%= "open" if open %>>
    <summary class="attachment-group-head">
      <%= label %> <span class="muted">(<%= rows.size %>)</span>
    </summary>
    <div class="attachments-grid">
      <% rows.each do |row| %>
        <% node = row.node %>
        <% ext = File.extname(node.name).delete(".").upcase.first(4) %>
        <div class="attachment-tile">
          <%# THE SAME TWO BUILDERS THE FILES PAGE USES (FilesHelper), which is the point: these
              tiles carry the identical right-click menu, and written out here they were a fifth
              copy of one seven-key wire contract free to drift from the four over there.
              @addon_origins is keyed on node_id, so one lookup serves both — but the builder takes
              the ORIGIN, not the ivar, so a surface without one can still adopt it. %>
          <%= link_to file_path(row.node_id), class: "grid-card file-cell",
                      data: thumb_cell_data(row.node_id, ext)
                              .merge(file_menu_data(row.node_id, @addon_origins[row.node_id])) do %>
            <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: @page_thumbs.thumb(row.node_id), ext_label: ext %>
            <span class="grid-name"><%= node.name %></span>
          <% end %>
          <% if row.linked? %>
            <div class="tile-meta">
              <%= button_to "Detach", attachment_path(row.attachment), method: :delete, class: "btn small danger tile-detach",
                            form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Detach #{node.name}? (the file itself is kept)" } } %>
              <%= button_to "Move into project", relocate_project_attachments_path(@project),
                            params: { node_id: row.node_id }, class: "btn small tile-move" %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
